+
+## Unsmell run 2026-11-01 (third pass): prompter bridge and demo installer
+
+- [ ] `internal/proxy/prompter.go` `newPrompterBridge` doc is four lines because one pointer carries three outcomes (nil, a bridge that serves nothing, a live bridge). It shrinks once the "two states behind one pointer" entry above is fixed. Three re-checks in a row disagreed on how to tell the nil case from the serves-nothing case. Both mean that another process owns the name, so the wording problem goes away once the return shape is fixed.
+- [ ] `internal/proxy/prompter.go` `prompterBridge` type doc (lines 23–46) is 24 lines of mechanism, history and a method list. Rewrite it as the bridge's place in the system in two or three sentences, and move the protocol walk-through to a design doc.
+- [ ] `internal/proxy/prompter.go` const-block doc (lines 12–15) opens with a sentence fragment and joins a second idea with a semicolon. `PromptDone` doc ends with gnome-keyring's reason for the call ("so it can tear the prompt down"), which belongs to the caller.
+- [ ] `internal/proxy/prompter_test.go` `mockShellPrompter` doc says the mock "can also drive the reverse Callback". It has no such method; the test calls the callback through `shellConn.Object`. `TestPrompterBridge` doc is seven lines; cut it to what the test covers.
+- [ ] `internal/proxy/forward.go:74` `nameHasOwner` turns a failed NameHasOwner call into false, so `newPrompterBridge` then tries to claim the name. Decide whether a failed check should be an error.
+- [ ] `e2e/gnome/vm/demo-driver-install.sh` header (lines 2–23) is 22 lines that narrate the phases. Line 5 says demo.sh relogs with `systemctl restart gdm`, but demo.sh:245–268 logs out through QMP and GDM TimedLogin. The "relogin is why recording is host-side" fact is repeated from demo.sh:28–30.
+- [ ] `demo-driver-install.sh` lines 33–85: `type_cmd`, `wait_for`, `owner_is`, `rd`, `place` and `open_window` are copies of `demo-driver.sh:21–75`. Move them into one sourced lib. In it, `open_window` should use `wait_for` instead of its own `seq 15` poll loop, and take the window rectangle so the four `open_window; sleep 1; place x y w h` sequences become one call.
+- [ ] `demo-driver-install.sh:141` and `demo-driver.sh:108` both build the rd_agent unlock batch (`waittext Unlock`, `type`, `key enter`, `waittext`/`clicktext <label>`) inline. Give it one helper, such as `unlock_and_click <label>`, in the shared lib.
+- [ ] The stash file `$HOME/secrets-dispatcher-fixed` is written by `demo.sh:153` and read by `demo-driver-install.sh:101`, `demo-driver.sh:88` and `demo.sh:313`. Give the path one owner. The owner-pid-and-readlink lookup in `demo-driver-install.sh:56–59` is also written in `demo.sh:304–308`.
+- [ ] `demo-driver-install.sh` comment style on unchanged lines: trailing comments on `type_cmd`, `wait_for`, `owner_is`, `open_window` and the comment above `place` open with the function's name; lines 91, 117, 125 and 132 join two ideas with a colon or semicolon; line 142's trailing comment is too long for the line; lines 144–145 have a comma splice.
